 "caption_proposed_tex": "\\caption{\\textbf{Descriptively, the crossing law recovers every slope class but predicts too shallow vision--language slopes, whereas the affine null N1 predicts every slope too steep (Theorem~\\ref{thm:crossing}).} (a--c) Class medians of mKNN at $k=10$ on nested COCO pools, observed and as predicted from the fit size. (d) Predicted against observed slope of $\\ln s_N$ on $\\ln m$ per pair, $\\pm1$ s.d.\\ over pool orderings. A pair has the right class where the grey bands cross or in the white lower left. The two long thin bars come from orderings where N1 is undefined. Tables~\\ref{tab:app-s11-classes} to~\\ref{tab:app-s11-sens} give the values.}",
